      "name": "warnings_when_merging_starts_and_when_caught_up"
    }
  ],
  "description": "The stream's delivery buffer under backpressure. input.limit is stream_backlog_limit; input.ops put a wire message (as received) or take n messages (as the consumer would); the rest is drained at the end. expected.delivered are the wire payloads in delivery order (a merged entry carries the merged fields), merged the number of messages merged into an earlier entry, warnings the backlog WARNINGs in order (merging_started when the first merge happens, caught_up when the backlog falls below half the limit). While >= limit messages wait, a tf / df of an instrument (e, tk) is merged into its newest waiting entry when that is a feed of the same type (rule a), or into its second-newest when that is a feed of the same type and the newest a feed of the other type, copying the fields the newest's type can carry into the newest too (rule b); otherwise it is appended. Acks, order / position updates and unknown messages are never merged, and nothing merges across an entry of the same instrument.",
  "source": "tradesmart.stream.delivery.DeliveryBuffer",
  "tolerance": {}
}
